---
title: Sourdough Loaf
cooklang: 2
yield: 900%g
makes: 1 loaf
unit system: metric
basis:
  flour:
    total: 500%g
    members: [bread flour, whole wheat flour]
time:
  prep: 40 minutes
  rest: 18 hours
  cook: 40 minutes
techniques: [autolyse, stretch and fold, shape, bake]
tags: [bread, sourdough, weekend]
---

= Levain ~{-1%day} -> levain

`Mix` @active starter{50%g} with @bread flour{50%g} and @water{50%g}(lukewarm) in a
#jar. Cover loosely.

`Rest` until ~{doubled and domed}, ~prove{8-12%hours} at room temperature.

= Dough -> dough

`Mix` @&bread flour{80%flour} and @whole wheat flour{20%flour} with @water{70%flour}(cool)
in a #large bowl{} until ~{no dry flour remains}. -> autolyse

`Rest` the @&autolyse{} for ~rest{45%minutes}.

`Add` @&levain{100%g} and @fine sea salt{2%flour} to the @&autolyse{} in the #&large bowl{}. Squeeze and fold
until ~{incorporated}.

`Stretch and fold` the @&dough{} in the bowl, four times, ~rest{30%minutes} apart.

`Bulk ferment 24 °C` ~prove{4-5%hours} at 24 °C, until ~{roughly 50 % larger and jiggly}.

= Shaping and proof ~{-12%hours}

`Shape` the @&dough{} into a tight round on a lightly floured #bench{}, seam side up into
a floured #banneton{}.

`Cold proof` in the #fridge{} for ~prove{12%hours}.

= Baking

`Preheat 250 °C` the #oven{} with a #dutch oven{} inside to 250 °C for ~oven{45%minutes}.

`Turn` the @&dough{} out into the hot #&dutch oven{} and `score` it with a #lame{} or razor,
one long cut at a shallow angle.

`Bake 230 °C covered` for ~oven{20%minutes}, then `bake uncovered` for ~oven{20-25%minutes}
until ~{deeply browned}.

`Cool` on a #rack{} for at least ~rest{1%hour}. Cut into @{12} slices.
